# Shell scripts run on Linux (VPS) or WSL — force LF regardless of the
# committer's OS. CRLF in a .sh file can break bash parsing in ways that
# are easy to miss locally (e.g. a stray \r before `{` in a multi-line
# function definition) but fail outright on the VPS. Discovered 2 Jul 2026
# when ops/deploy_vps.sh's committed blob turned out to be CRLF despite
# core.autocrlf=true, because the file predated any normalisation rule.
*.sh text eol=lf
